A||||10||Adrift||Car speakers with home stereo?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||10-21-2001||07:34 PM||||I'm just hooking up my stereo (installing 6 1/2's in the door) and want to test them out before I install them for good - is it okay to just hook them up to my home stereo to test them out?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Ari<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kasdan||10-21-2001||07:59 PM||||i dont see why not, in my Lumina Euro i hooked up some INfinity GOld bookshelf speakers behind the seats, so i would think it would be reversable.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">           <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-21-2001||08:19 PM||||careful... Car audio runs at 4ohms, home at 8 or 16...<P>You can wreck both the amp and the speaker if you aren't carful... Don't play them at ANY serious volume, or you will burn the amp and the voice coils.||||reg||4
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||10-21-2001||08:22 PM||||yup, exactly what Mach 10 says.  One trick would be to hook up your 2 car speakers in series, therefore the amp would see them as 8 ohm, which is the standard house speaker.  I know people who have done this with no problems, even at a decent volume.  best of luck to ya!<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||10-21-2001||09:10 PM||||If you have a good home stereo system you can push 4 ohms. I have a pair of EPI speakers that are 2 ohms each!<P>Maybe if you hook them up to a k-mart special boom box it will toast it though...||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroRacer||10-22-2001||12:45 AM||||I hooked up a Pioneer 5x7 From the daytona to my Klipsch ProMedia 4.1 as an experiment.  All I can say is when those 60w rms hit that Pioneer, it sounded a hell of alot better then in the daytona  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Hippocrat||10-22-2001||02:54 AM||||Yep nothing like the smell of a couple of roasting speakers. I remember the days lol <P>And of course thank God for overload protection on most of todays amps.<P>But a lot of subs these days are rated 4 or 8 ohms Id want to be sure though. My Cerwins are.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||10-22-2001||03:04 AM||||Yeah, sorry, should have stated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>A lot of new home-amps can and do rate down to 2 ohms. This however is unusual. Most newer ones have overload protection. Don't count on it saving BOTH the speaker and the amp. <P>Master_sushi: EPIs?!? Damn! I thought *I* was the only one with a set  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> No idea what models. They're a 4-way tower. Sound great, even though they don't suck power  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Hippocrat||10-22-2001||04:10 AM||||Overload protection did save my amp but those poor unfortunate 6 x 9s well to this day I can smell them cooking.<P>So I definitely agree I would never count on it saving both the amp and the speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||10-22-2001||02:59 PM||||EPI's are pretty good speakers. They were some of the best you could get at the time they were made. They might not be up to todays standards but they still sound great. They are known for great midrange sound. Depending on what models you have, and if they have the orignal drivers. Take out ony of the speakers in the case and look at the size of the magnet! They are HUGE square ones, even the tweeter has a biger magnet then allot of woffers made now. They cost a bit when they were new, I think mine were about 1K each pair when they first came out.<BR>Heres a pic I got off the net of mine...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/epi.JPG">   <P>Oh, and when I mean quality amps I mean really good pro stuff. I listen to a pair of new Bose 901s' with a briged Rotel mono amp on each one, pushing about 350watts rms each side, with a powered 250watt rms 12 inch sub. This is real watts also, not computer speakers P.M.P.O., or ebay "pyramid amps" pushing 1500 watts for $50    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.. hehe<P>{Sorry if this was off topic, but home stereos have allways been one of my big hobbies!}<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||Mach10||10-22-2001||03:53 PM||||hehehehehehe I HAVE one of those 1500W Pyramid amps. Well, at least my brother does, but he gave up using it, and it's in my closet (don't know why). The only thing I'd consider using it for is as a linear-amplfyer to scramble Radar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Nope, those EPIs are original. Some friends of the family moved, and left a storage locker full for like 7 years, then handed us the keys and told us to keep whatever we want, and burn the rest. I snagged a turntable and those EPIs. The mid-range and highs on those things are incredible, even WITH a shitty amp. ||||reg||10
